NAME: Capacity board
OWNER: Ops
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 5:57 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Capacity board" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Capacity board · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Capacity board · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Capacity board · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Capacity board · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Capacity board · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ops/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-ops.md yet, record it with the capacity-board skill (recompute the sha256 of the pending item's payload and match it to the decision's HASH; yes: note it and tell TMEC Command to carry it out; no: mark it declined; change: refile once as a new item), then add its id and the outcome to the sent keys so it is never read twice. TMEC Command may already have nudged you in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), write the board and notes only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-ops/ and do it first (a "how fast?" question is answered with the capacity-board skill, never from yesterday's board).
Then use the capacity-board skill to rebuild /workspace/tmec-team/data/ops/capacity.md from the schedule read now. If `schedule` is missing from /workspace/tmec-team/context/config.json, or the source can't be read, write the board with status UNKNOWN and the reason, and put one question for Tommy in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/ops/ as item ops-<today>-schedule in the item format (once, not every run). This report always goes out, so never write NO_CHANGE.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/ops.md: the status line, the earliest slot per team (or UNKNOWN), the sold-not-scheduled count, anything blocked and why. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy.
